        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5c93bb9b-3b14-52e7-9064-ce5a54bab0d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Sikoryak, Samuel Beckett\n- Projects: Masterpiece Comics, Carousel\n- Works: Waiting for Godot, Crime and Punishment, Dostoyevsky Comics, Waiting to Go\n- Characters: Vladimir, Estragon, Godot, Raskol, Daria Morgendorffer\n- Series: Beavis and Butt-Head, Daria, Batman\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Sikoryak, born in 1964, is an American artist who usually signs his work as R. Sikoryak.\n- Samuel Beckett wrote Waiting for Godot, a play in which Vladimir and Estragon wait for someone named Godot who never arrives while encountering other characters and talking.\n- Since 1997, Robert Sikoryak has hosted Carousel, a long-running multimedia comics slide show presented at venues across the United States and Canada.\n- Robert Sikoryak specializes in comic adaptations of literary classics.\n- Under the title Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak adapted Crime and Punishment in the style of Bob Kane-era Batman as Dostoyevsky Comics, starring Raskol.\n- Under Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak also mixed Waiting for Godot with Beavis and Butt-Head to create Waiting to Go.\n- Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series Beavis and Butt-Head and its spin-off Daria.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f75c0329-15a3-523d-bc56-8e6cc043d4f7",
        "text": "Page: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Robert Sikoryak (born 1964) is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: He specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics\", these include \"Crime and Punishment\" rendered in Bob Kane–era Batman style, becoming \"Dostoyevsky Comics\", starring Raskol; and \"Waiting for Godot\" mixed with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\", becoming \"Waiting to Go\".\nPage: Waiting for Godot. Sentence: Waiting for Godot ( ) is a play by Samuel Beckett, in which two characters, Vladimir and Estragon, wait for the arrival of someone named Godot who never arrives, and while waiting they engage in a variety of discussions and encounter three other characters.\nPage: Carousel (comics). Sentence: Carousel is a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak (\"Masterpiece Comics\") that has been presented in various venues in the United States and Canada since 1997.\nPage: Daria Morgendorffer. Sentence: Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series \"Beavis and Butt-Head\" and its spin-off \"Daria\".",
